<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">At-Turaif</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as al-Turaif, Turaif District</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">At-Turaif is the historic citadel district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a>, which served as the seat of the first Saudi state in the 18th and early 19th centuries. Its mud-brick palaces, mosques and houses are a leading example of the Najdi architectural style. Ruined after the Ottoman-Egyptian siege of 1818, it was inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2010 and has since been extensively restored.</p></div>
